{"id":"1d2ca19e714484a36c761f2ac5846314af3d982c","url":"https://www.theverge.com/tech/988172/anker-mammotion-robot-mowers-edgers-ifa-2026","title":"These new robot lawn mowers trim your edges","site_name":"TechURLs","source":"The Verge","byline":"Emma Roth","excerpt":"At IFA 2026, Anker and Mammotion took the wraps off their newest robot lawnmowers, both of which come with an edger attachment to clean up the sides of your driveway and garden beds.","content_html":"<DIV class=\"page\" id=\"readability-page-1\"><div id=\"zephr-anchor\"><p>Anker’s new robot lawn mower might take over for your Weedwacker, too. Announced at IFA 2026, the Eufy Robot Lawn Mower S2 Max comes with an extendable trimming arm to clean up the grass around your driveway and flowerbeds.</p><p>The dual-blade mower offers vSLAM navigation that uses built-in cameras to build a 3D map of your yard, eliminating the need to set up boundary wires or a real-time kinematic (RTK) base station. Anker says the Mower S2 Max can map and mow up to 3.7 acres, while handling yards with up to 80 percent (38-degree) slopes. The robot mower is AWD and will launch in May 2027 for €3,999. There’s no word on US pricing or availability yet.</p><section tabindex=\"-1\" aria-label=\"carousel\"><div id=\":R36bcprar96:\"><p><a href=\"https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/09/S2-Max-Mower-on-grass.jpg?quality=90&strip=all\" data-pswp-height=\"1416\" data-pswp-width=\"1212\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer\"><img alt=\"<em>The</em> <em>Eufy Robot Lawn Mower S2 Max</em>.\" data-chromatic=\"ignore\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-nimg=\"fill\" sizes=\"(max-width: 1023px) 100vw, 744px\" srcSet=\"https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/09/S2-Max-Mower-on-grass.jpg?quality=90&strip=all&w=376 376w, https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/09/S2-Max-Mower-on-grass.jpg?quality=90&strip=all&w=384 384w, https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/